      { text: 'First get one row per player with their attempt count. Then add a column that places each player on a 0-to-1 scale by that count — and be deliberate about which column the ranking is ordered by (activity, not id).', starterCode: '-- Step 1: one row per player with their attempt count\nWITH attempt_counts AS (\n  SELECT user_id, COUNT(*) AS total_attempts\n  FROM level_attempts\n  GROUP BY user_id\n)\n-- Step 2: add the percentile column (0..1), rounded to 2, named pct_rank.\n-- Order the ranking by activity. Final rows ordered by user_id.\nSELECT user_id, total_attempts,\n  -- your percentile expression here\nFROM attempt_counts\nORDER BY user_id' }
