    estimatedMin: 8,
    datamartId: 'food_delivery',
    prompt: 'The restaurant operations team at DoorDash is investigating why Chicago restaurants are being flagged for slow food preparation times, despite managers claiming their kitchen ticket times are under 25 minutes. The report uses the \'avg_prep_min\' column, but there is a suspicion that this metric is being calculated incorrectly. Identify the issue with the current metric definition and correct it.',
    brokenQuery: 'SELECT\n  ROUND(AVG(\n    (julianday(delivered_at) - julianday(accepted_at)) * 24 * 60\n  )) AS avg_prep_min\nFROM orders\nWHERE status = \'delivered\'',
    brokenOutputNote: 'Returns 51. The metric computes minutes from order acceptance to customer delivery — this includes both food preparation AND courier travel time. Restaurant prep ends when the courier picks up the order (picked_up_at). The correct metric is accepted_at → picked_up_at, not accepted_at → delivered_at.',
